25,2,1,talk,Mio,,"Transport costs vary wildly depending on distance, and whole-building lets have non-refundable deposits if people drop out.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
26,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems mixing happens during shared evenings, but some members never even attend the away camps.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
27,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Public bookings are a lottery nightmare with huge applications, and cooking for ourselves on campus is a huge time sink.","{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
28,2,1,talk,Rin,,"The inland clubs had eight people per room and strict lights-out! Also, our own hall is already quite crowded.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
29,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"Public beds are cheap, but a third of our members can't even reach campus by nine without staying overnight.","{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
30,2,2,talk,Mio,,That's a lot of risk with the deposits. We should be careful about where we commit.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"If we want the club to bond, we must ensure everyone stays together in one place.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,The administrative burden of public centers sounds excessive. We need something more efficient for the organizers.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,2,talk,Rin,,Eight people to a room sounds exhausting. I don't think we'll get any rest there.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"The budget is tight, and the logistics of getting everyone to campus are more complicated than they look.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
